\title{Performance and Benchmarking}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    What actually costs time, and how to read a published comparison. The target is a cost model good enough to predict the direction of a change before measuring it.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The cost breakdown: witness generation, hashing, FFTs, MSMs, extension-field arithmetic.}
        \li{Cycles per second as a metric, and what it hides — precompiles, [shard](dhsorens-003O) size, security parameters.}
        \li{Proof size and verifier time across systems, and the recursion that produces the final numbers.}
        \li{How the [field choice](dhsorens-002K) shows up in measurements, and why hash rate is often the real headline.}
        \li{Comparing at equal security: the benchmark question that is usually skipped.}
    }
}

\p{
    Sources: [zkvm-benchmarks](https://github.com/a16z/zkvm-benchmarks).
}
